## Objective

Make the app-server-backed behavior shipped by T002/T006/T007 the documented and diagnosable managed Codex path. Operators and agents must be able to identify the active transport, its lifecycle, its DND/composer deferral behavior, and the hook fallback without an opt-in profile or hand-edited configuration.

## Scope and non-goals

- Update public/reference docs, install output, status/instances output, and `c2c doctor` capability reporting for the canonical managed path.
- This is documentation and diagnostics work. Do not add a second "safe profile," change command grammar, or implement delivery policy here.
- Preserve ordinary Codex hooks as the unmanaged/unsupported-version fallback and describe `hooks+wake` truthfully as an input-injecting mode.

## References

- Implemented behavior receipts: T004 and T007 `.collab/research/` artifacts
- Research: `.collab/research/2026-07-11-codex-app-server-safe-delivery.md`
- Documentation rules: `.collab/runbooks/documentation-hygiene.md`, `docs/CLAUDE.md`, `docs/clients/feature-matrix.md`, `docs/clients/e2e-checklist.md`, `docs/get-started.md`, and `docs/commands.md`
- Current operational surfaces: `ocaml/cli/c2c_doctor_cmd.ml`, `ocaml/cli/c2c_doctor_hooks.ml`, `ocaml/cli/c2c_instances_cmd.ml`, `ocaml/cli/test_c2c_doctor_hooks.ml`, and `ocaml/test/test_c2c_doctor_capabilities.ml`
- DND contract: `docs/dnd-mode-spec.md`
- Approval isolation: `ocaml/cli/c2c_approval_paths.ml`, `ocaml/cli/c2c_approval_cmd.ml`, and `ocaml/cli/test_c2c_approval_paths.ml`
- Official app-server and hook docs: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/app-server and https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks

## State and ownership boundaries

- T006 owns command names, flags, alias generation, resume, and process lifecycle; T007 owns auto-turn/deferral policy; B127 owns offline queue semantics.
- Doctor/status may observe and explain app-server endpoint health, TUI attachment, DND, and delivery mode, but must not mutate them.
- Never print socket credentials, authentication tokens, message bodies, or composer contents. Redact private endpoint components if required by the T001 boundary.

## Acceptance criteria

- Managed `c2c start codex` is documented as canonical, with generated alias default, optional `--alias`, `--yolo` warning, `new`/`resume`/shortcut grammar, TUI-exit lifecycle, and offline behavior exactly matching T006/B127.
- Docs replace the broad B098 statement with the implemented rule: eligible local broker mail can cause a Codex turn; message content still cannot resolve approvals or write verdict files. Relay policy and trust boundaries are explicit.
- DND, non-empty/unknown composer state, active-turn batching, and idle behavior match T007 verbatim enough to be operationally testable.
- `c2c doctor` and machine-readable output distinguish at least: healthy app-server remote TUI, app-server unavailable/incompatible, hooks-only fallback, and legacy `hooks+wake` input injection. Each degraded state includes an actionable remediation.
- Install/status/instances output uses the same delivery-mode vocabulary and never claims instant delivery when only a hook boundary is available.
- Transport guidance defaults to the proven local boundary from T001. Any TCP/WebSocket guidance requires authentication and explicit exposure warnings; no unauthenticated listener is recommended.
- Command/help examples are copied from tested commands, and docs contain links to official app-server/hooks references for version drift.

## Deliverables and receipts

- Updated public docs, AGENTS/runbooks where policy changed, doctor/status/install tests, and generated docs if the repository workflow requires them.
- A docs/diagnostics receipt listing every changed surface, tested output snippets, supported Codex version/capabilities, and links to T004/T007 evidence.

## Verification

```sh
just build
just check
dune exec --root "$PWD" ocaml/cli/test_c2c_doctor_hooks.exe
dune exec --root "$PWD" ocaml/test/test_c2c_doctor_capabilities.exe
```

Also run the repository's docs build/check command named by `docs/CLAUDE.md`, plus focused tests for any changed install/status/instances module.

## Blockers

P1.M1.E1.T004 and T007 must supply live behavioral receipts; P1.M1.E1.T006 must freeze the public grammar and lifecycle before documentation is finalized.
